      "step": 14,
      "user_message": "What did we decide on for my new plant to grow at home? Can you please help me recall?",
      "expected_behavior": "Agent should recall from memory: Plant Name",
      "agent_response": "You chose to grow sweet basil at home.\n\nQuick refresher and next steps:\n- Light: 6–8 hours of bright light (south/southwest-facing window or a grow light).\n- Pot & soil: 6–8\" pot with good drainage and a light, well-draining potting mix.\n- Water: Keep soil evenly moist but not waterlogged; water when top 1/2\" feels dry.\n- Temperature: Prefers 65–80°F; protect from drafts and cold.\n- Feeding: Light balanced fertilizer every 4–6 weeks or a diluted liquid feed.\n- Pruning/harvest: Pinch flower buds and regularly harvest leaves to encourage bushier growth.\n- Pests: Watch for aphids, whiteflies, and fungal issues; good airflow helps prevent problems.\n\nWould you like me to:\n- Find nearby nurseries or online seed sources,\n- Draft a shopping list for pot/soil/seeds,\n- Set a recurring watering reminder,\nor\n- Add a short care guide to your calendar or notes?",
