    {
      "step": 15,
      "user_message": "Can you help me recall the school event game we decided on for my event?",
      "expected_behavior": "Agent should recall from memory: \"school event game\"",
      "agent_response": "I don't have a record of a specific school-event game decision in your saved notes. Did we decide that elsewhere (email, calendar, or a different note)? If you want, I can search your emails or draft notes for it — tell me where to look.\n\nIf you don't have the exact one saved, here are quick game options that work well for school events (pick by age, space, and tone):\n\n- Scavenger hunt — great for mixed ages, can be themed and run indoors/outdoors.  \n- Relay races (sack race, three-legged, egg-and-spoon) — energetic, outdoor, simple setup.  \n- Minute-to-Win-It challenges — lots of quick rounds, good for small teams.  \n- Trivia / Kahoot quiz — low setup, works well indoors with teams.  \n- Obstacle course — adaptable for space and skill levels.  \n- Bingo with school-themed cards — calm, inclusive, easy to run.  \n- Human knot / team-building challenges — good for cooperation and small groups.  \n- Escape-room-style puzzle stations — higher prep, very engaging for older kids.  \n\nTell me:\n- Age/grade range, \n- Indoor or outdoor, \n- Number of participants, and \n- Whether you want competitive or cooperative activities.\n\nI’ll recommend the best fit and can create rules, materials list, timing, and prize ideas — or search your email/calendar for any earlier decision. Which would you like?",
      "duration_s": 13.183,
      "passed": false,
